The limitation period does not apply to: 

requirements for the protection of personal non-property rights and other intangible bene ts, except as provided by law; 

claims of depositors to the bank for the issuance of deposits, as well as claims to the Deposit Guarantee Agency for the payment of compensation on a guaranteed deposit; 

claims for compensation for harm caused to the life or health of a citizen. Claims led after the expiration of the limitation period shall be satis ed no more than three years prior to the ling of the claim; 

claims for compensation for damage caused by the crime; 

the demands of the owner or other owner to eliminate any violations of his right, although 

these violations were not related to deprivation of possession ( <u>A  rticle 231 (show_doc.fwx? rgn  =767#A000000237)</u> of this Code); 

demands for the return of property of historical, cultural, scienti c and artistic value, and other valuable objects taken out of the country before the declaration of its independence; 

other requirements in cases established by law. 

