## **Article 248** 

The amount of a payment made, insufficient for the full performance of a monetary obligation, in the absence of another agreement shall first of all discharge the creditor's costs of obtaining performance, then interest, and in the remaining part the principal amount of the debt, except for the cases provided for by part two of this article. 

If the amount of a payment made is insufficient for the performance of obligations under a micro-loan or credit extended to a borrower who is an individual or a borrower who is a business entity, the borrower's debt shall be discharged in the following order: 

1) proportionately, overdue principal debt and overdue interest payments; 

2) accrued interest for the current period and principal debt for the current period; 

3) penalties (fines, late fees); 

4) other expenses of the creditor related to the discharge of the debt.

