# **§ 309 Termination of guarantee** 

The obligation of the guarantor to the bene ciary under the guarantee shall terminate: 

1) payment to the bene ciary of the amount for which the guarantee was issued; 

2) the end of the period speci ed in the guarantee for which it was issued; 

3) due to the refusal of the bene ciary of his rights under the guarantee and its return to the guarantor; 

4) due to the waiver of the bene ciary of his rights under the guarantee by a written statement on the release of the guarantor from his obligations. 

Termination of a guarantor's obligation on the grounds speci ed in <u>p  arag  rap  hs 1</u> = = <u>( show_doc.fwx?r gn 767#B3YB102ZR9) , 2 (show_d  oc.fwx? r gn 767#B3YB10378S)</u> and <u>4</u> = <u>o  f part o  ne o  f (s  ho  w_do  c.fwx?rgn 767#B3YB103LUU)</u> this article does not depend on whether 

the guarantee has been returned to him. 

The guarantor who has become aware of the termination of the guarantee must notify the principal without delay.

