## **Article 318** 

The rights of the creditor under the obligation are transferred to another person: 

1) as a result of universal legal succession in the rights of the creditor; 

2) by a court decision on the transfer of the creditor's rights to another person; 

3) as a result of the performance of the obligation of the debtor by his guarantor or the pledgor who is not a debtor under this obligation; 

4) upon subrogation (transfer) to the insurer of the rights of the creditor in relation to the debtor responsible for the occurrence of the insured event; 

5) in other cases provided for by law.

